# Rust
/target/
**/target/
debug/
*.rs.bk
*.rlib
*.prof*

# Node / TypeScript
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm/
# Root dev-tooling lockfile (lint/format only; installed with `npm install`, not pinned).
/package-lock.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Go
*.exe
*.test
*.out
/vendor/

# WASM / build artifacts
pkg/
*.wasm

# Native FFI build outputs
*.dylib
*.so
*.a
*.dll
*.node

# Compiled demo binary (build artifact, not source)
/examples/go_demo/cleverbase-go-demo

# Coverage
coverage/
*.profraw
lcov.info

# Generated API documentation. The Markdown under docs/api/ IS committed (so the reference docs are
# browseable on GitHub) and regenerated by scripts/gen-docs.sh / `make docs`; the docs workflow
# checks it stays in sync. Only the build INTERMEDIATES are ignored: the rustdoc HTML/JSON dumps
# (target/doc, already covered by /target above) and any stray HTML a generator might emit.
target/doc/
/docs/api/**/*.html
/docs/api/**/*.json

# Env / secrets (never commit Cleverbase client secrets, TSA creds, etc.)
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Generated test-PKI artifacts. The synthetic test material is committed as DER / PKCS#8
# (*.der, *.pk8); the openssl integration tests materialize any PEMs they need into a per-call
# temp dir, so these mutable openssl bookkeeping files must never be tracked.
/tests/fixtures/pki/*.srl
/tests/fixtures/pki/*serial*

# EUDI attestation test fixtures (feature 004). Same convention as tests/fixtures/pki: the durable
# tracked material is the DER certs (*.cert.der) + PKCS#8 keys (*.key.pk8) + the JSON/YAML/Kotlin
# vectors + trust-list.json + NOTICE + gen.sh; the *.srl serial byproduct of `openssl x509 -CA` is
# transient and must never be tracked (the *.pem/*.key working files are already dropped above).
/tests/fixtures/attestation/*.srl

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.tmp
